          {
            "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Df14XPmF2yj/",
            "label": "🎙️ A new episode of Pirate Perspectives is here!⁠ <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.ncmissouri.edu/wp-content/plugins/instagram-feed/img/placeholder.png\" alt=\"🎙️ A new episode of Pirate Perspectives is here!⁠ ⁠ We&#039;re celebrating International Education Week (November 16–20) on this episode by highlighting some of the international students who make NCMC&#039;s campus community so unique! 🌎🏴‍☠️⁠ ⁠ In Episode 12, host Nicole Shell sits down with Jamie Cunningham, NCMC&#039;s International Student Representative, and international students Riky Staurenghi, Alejandro Somaza Silva, and Melaku Simon.⁠ ⁠ Hear about their journeys to NCMC, adjusting to life in Missouri, balancing academics and athletics, and the friendships and experiences that have made NCMC feel like home. Jamie also shares stories from her international recruitment travels and how she helps students navigate their college experience.⁠ ⁠ From cultural differences and Missouri weather to favorite foods and future goals, this episode celebrates the diverse backgrounds and perspectives our international students bring to the Pirate community!⁠ ⁠ 🎧 Tune in to Episode 12 of Pirate Perspectives: https://www.buzzsprout.com/admin/2536323/episodes/20129028-pirate-perspectives-episode-12-international-students ⁠ ⁠ You can also find Pirate Perspectives on Apple Podcasts and Spotify—just search Pirate Perspectives and hit Follow so you never miss an episode! 🎧⁠ ⁠ Whether you&#039;re from just down the road or halfway around the world, we&#039;re glad you&#039;re part of the Pirate family! ❤️🖤⁠ ⁠ #NCMCPirates #PiratePerspectives #InternationalEducationWeek #InternationalStudents\" aria-hidden=\"true\">"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Df0KgWmlxbz/",
            "label": "BINGO NIGHT AT NCMC!⁠ ⁠ 🏴‍☠️ Calling all Pirates! <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.ncmissouri.edu/wp-content/plugins/instagram-feed/img/placeholder.png\" alt=\"BINGO NIGHT AT NCMC!⁠ ⁠ 🏴‍☠️ Calling all Pirates! Whether you live on campus or commute to NCMC, you&#039;re invited to join us for a fun night of BINGO!⁠ ⁠ Grab your friends, test your luck, and see if you can shout BINGO before anyone else! 🎱⁠ ⁠ 📅 Thursday, November 19, 2026⁠ ⏰ 7:00 PM⁠ 📍 Nuttall Student Center⁠ ⁠ This is a great opportunity to take a break from studying, meet other students, and enjoy some friendly competition!⁠ ⁠ ❤️🖤 Residential students AND commuters — we hope to see you there!⁠ ⁠ #NCMCPirates #NCMCStudentLife #BingoNight #PiratePride\" aria-hidden=\"true\">"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Dfz19BwFxJb/",
            "label": "North Central Missouri College and Ketcham Center <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.ncmissouri.edu/wp-content/plugins/instagram-feed/img/placeholder.png\" alt=\"North Central Missouri College and Ketcham Center Closed for Thanksgiving⁠ ⁠ All North Central Missouri College campuses will be closed Wednesday, November 25-Friday, November 27, in observance of the Thanksgiving holiday. No on-ground classes will be held, and all offices will be closed. North Central Missouri College will reopen on Monday, November 30, for regular business hours. For more information about NCMC holiday hours, contact 660-359-3948.⁠ ⁠ The Ketcham Community Center hours on Wednesday, November 25, will be 6:00 a.m. until 6:00 p.m. and will be closed on Thursday, November 27, and Friday, November 27 6:00 a.m.-12:00 p.m. On Saturday, November 28, and Sunday, November 29, KCC will be open during regular hours. For more information about the Ketcham Community Center, contact 660-359-3948 x1450. ⁠\" aria-hidden=\"true\">"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DfzacN9l9Cg/",
            "label": "🌎Celebrating International Education Week!⁠ ⁠ Nove <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.ncmissouri.edu/wp-content/plugins/instagram-feed/img/placeholder.png\" alt=\"🌎Celebrating International Education Week!⁠ ⁠ November 16–20 is International Education Week, and NCMC is proud to celebrate the diverse cultures, experiences, and perspectives that our international students bring to campus!⁠ ⁠ Did you know NCMC currently has students enrolled from 9 different countries? 🇨🇴 🇻🇪 🇩🇴 🇹🇴 🇬🇧 🇮🇹 🇨🇼 🇲🇽 🇪🇸⁠ ⁠ Our international students represent Colombia, Venezuela, the Dominican Republic, Tonga, England, Italy, Curaçao, Mexico, and Spain!⁠ ⁠ These students enrich our campus community by sharing their unique backgrounds, traditions, and experiences while pursuing their educational goals at NCMC.⁠ ⁠ 🎙️ Be sure to check back tomorrow for a new episode of Pirate Perspectives! This month&#039;s episode features NCMC&#039;s International Student Representative and three of our international students as they share their experiences studying in the United States and being part of the NCMC community.⁠ ⁠ Join us in celebrating the connections, friendships, and opportunities that international education brings to NCMC! ❤️🖤⁠ ⁠ #InternationalEducationWeek #NCMCPirates #PiratePerspectives #InternationalStudents #GlobalEducation\" aria-hidden=\"true\">"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DfsH1ful6Cy/",
            "label": "🎓 Celebrating Academic Excellence at NCMC Savannah <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.ncmissouri.edu/wp-content/plugins/instagram-feed/img/placeholder.png\" alt=\"🎓 Celebrating Academic Excellence at NCMC Savannah! ❤️🖤⁠ ⁠ Congratulations to three outstanding NCMC students who were recently inducted into the Phi Theta Kappa (PTK) Honor Society during a special ceremony at our Savannah Campus on November 10!⁠ ⁠ 👏 Please join us in celebrating our newest PTK members:⁠ ⁠ ⭐ Jenna Gray – Cameron, MO⁠ ⁠ ⭐ Mariana Pablo – St. Joseph, MO⁠ ⁠ ⭐ Izabella Walker – Skidmore, MO⁠ ⁠ Phi Theta Kappa recognizes academic excellence among two-year college students and provides opportunities for scholarships, leadership development, and community service. Students must achieve a GPA of 3.50 or higher and meet additional eligibility requirements to receive an invitation to join.⁠ ⁠ We are proud of these students for their hard work, dedication, and commitment to academic success! We can&#039;t wait to see what they accomplish next!⁠ ⁠ 📖 Read the full story: https://www.ncmissouri.edu/phi-theta-kappa-honor-society/⁠ ⁠ #NCMCPirates #NCMCSavannah #PhiThetaKappa #AcademicExcellence #StudentSuccess\" aria-hidden=\"true\">"
          },
